    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d425">

                <pb facs="0504" n="400" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg400"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4313: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-19T20:00:00+08:00">February 19, 1932—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 19—1:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Captain Mayer together with British Military Attaché and representatives of
                    French and Italian forces called on General Tsai Ting-kai to protest against
                    Chinese artillery fire into Yangtzepoo and to request that he refrain from
                    further fire in that direction. Tsai stated fire was in reply to Japanese
                    artillery fire from Settlement area and that he would definitely refrain from
                    such fire tonight and if assured by neutral observers and his own investigators
                    that no Japanese artillery <pb facs="0505" n="401" xml:id="pg401"/> was in
                    position in Settlement area he would never again fire there. He asked whether,
                    if Japanese wished to use neutral defense areas or Soochow Creek in front of
                    neutral defense areas as a position from which to attack Chinese, the neutral
                    powers would prevent the Japanese. I have referred these questions to the
                    commander in chief.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
